    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.cmdline\r\n\r\n### Question\r\n\r\nis it possible to configure mini.cmdline to go up/down through the list using Tab and S-Tab similar to how the wildmenu works? the current default is C-p and C-n but i can't figure out where that is getting mapped. I started with the mini.max configuration.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.cmdline</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">is it possible to configure mini.cmdline to go up/down through the list using Tab and S-Tab similar to how the wildmenu works? the current default is C-p and C-n but i can't figure out where that is getting mapped. I started with the mini.max configuration.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.cmdline\nQuestion\nis it possible to configure mini.cmdline to go up/down through the list using Tab and S-Tab similar to how the wildmenu works? the current default is C-p and C-n but i can't figure out where that is getting mapped. I started with the mini.max configuration.",
