    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Both `<Tab>` and `<S-Tab>` for default wildmenu navigation work with 'mini.cmdline', since its capabilities are built around wildmenu. I've tested with fresh MiniMax installation (both Neovim 0.11 and 0.12 Nightly) and in my own config.\r\n\r\nCould you please elaborate on how those keys don't work in Command line mode?\r\n\r\n> the current default is C-p and C-n but i can't figure out where that is getting mapped. I started with the mini.max configuration.\r\n\r\nThose are default ways of navigating up and down of both wildmenu (Command line completion) and Insert mode completion. See `:h c_CTRL-P` and `:h c_CTRL-N`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Both <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;Tab&gt;</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;S-Tab&gt;</code> for default wildmenu navigation work with 'mini.cmdline', since its capabilities are built around wildmenu. I've tested with fresh MiniMax installation (both Neovim 0.11 and 0.12 Nightly) and in my own config.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Could you please elaborate on how those keys don't work in Command line mode?</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">the current default is C-p and C-n but i can't figure out where that is getting mapped. I started with the mini.max configuration.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Those are default ways of navigating up and down of both wildmenu (Command line completion) and Insert mode completion. See <code class=\"notranslate\">:h c_CTRL-P</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">:h c_CTRL-N</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Both <Tab> and <S-Tab> for default wildmenu navigation work with 'mini.cmdline', since its capabilities are built around wildmenu. I've tested with fresh MiniMax installation (both Neovim 0.11 and 0.12 Nightly) and in my own config.\nCould you please elaborate on how those keys don't work in Command line mode?\n\nthe current default is C-p and C-n but i can't figure out where that is getting mapped. I started with the mini.max configuration.\n\nThose are default ways of navigating up and down of both wildmenu (Command line completion) and Insert mode completion. See :h c_CTRL-P and :h c_CTRL-N.",
