                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "thanks for clarifying the expected behavior. I went through each of my commits until I found when mini.cmdline stopped working correctly. Blink.cmp was a dependency for another plugin I was interested in using, and by default, Blink provides completion for cmdline which I was not aware.  Disabling blink.cmp allows mini.cmdline to work as expected. \r\n\r\nThanks so much for the time you've spent on mini.max. I've made excellent progress on creating my own nvim configuration after having given up many times in the past. ",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">thanks for clarifying the expected behavior. I went through each of my commits until I found when mini.cmdline stopped working correctly. Blink.cmp was a dependency for another plugin I was interested in using, and by default, Blink provides completion for cmdline which I was not aware.  Disabling blink.cmp allows mini.cmdline to work as expected.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks so much for the time you've spent on mini.max. I've made excellent progress on creating my own nvim configuration after having given up many times in the past.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "thanks for clarifying the expected behavior. I went through each of my commits until I found when mini.cmdline stopped working correctly. Blink.cmp was a dependency for another plugin I was interested in using, and by default, Blink provides completion for cmdline which I was not aware.  Disabling blink.cmp allows mini.cmdline to work as expected.\nThanks so much for the time you've spent on mini.max. I've made excellent progress on creating my own nvim configuration after having given up many times in the past.",
